function importGuide(){modal('Drawing scale + shared coordinates',`<h3>PDF / image</h3><p>Choose the page, place it, then pick the two ends of a known dimension and enter its real length in the displayed units. PDF page size or a printed “1:100” label is not sufficient after cropping or resizing. Verify a second known dimension before tracing. AI recognition interprets rooms, corridors and furniture separately. Trace image / PDF linework is only a raw tracing aid, not architectural recognition. Vector PDFs supply editable paths; JPG / PNG and scans generate editable centerline vectors, including angled and curved strokes. Review gaps, text and furniture, then correct missing or mistaken geometry with the drawing tools.</p><h3>DWG / Rhino 3DM</h3><p>Use 1:1 model-space 2D curves on XY, with explicit units. Select one floor and relevant layers; export surfaces/meshes as plan curves first. Curves are tessellated. Unsupported entities are listed in the import dialog. Keep the same origin and orientation for all floors and site. Coordinates are preserved by default; moving individual drawings to their own origins destroys registration.</p><h3>Single-line walls</h3><p>Select the wall-centerline layer, choose Single-line walls, and enter wall thickness. Door arcs and furniture belong on reference layers, not wall layers. Place functional Door / Exit openings after conversion.</p><h3>Double-line walls</h3><p>Choose Double-line faces to preview conservative straight-wall pairs. Set the expected thickness range and review each proposed centerline. Ambiguous, curved, short or substantially mismatched faces stay as reference. You can trace wall centerlines using Osnap. Door symbols are not automatically usable doors.</p><h3>Different origins / PDF floors</h3><p>Calibrate first. Use Align floor and pick the same two column-grid intersections in the current and reference floors. The app computes translation and rotation; it never aligns by outline centers. Cantilevers and setbacks retain their dimensions.</p><p class="callout">CAD limits: 35 MB / 35,000 reference segments / 1,500 wall segments per conversion. Export a clean plan with unnecessary hatches, annotation and 3D geometry removed.</p>`);}

function arrow(a,b,v,color){if(!a||!b)return;const p=w2s(a,v),q=w2s(b,v),ang=Math.atan2(q.y-p.y,q.x-p.x);ctx.fillStyle=color;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(q.x,q.y);ctx.lineTo(q.x-8*Math.cos(ang-.4),q.y-8*Math.sin(ang-.4));ctx.lineTo(q.x-8*Math.cos(ang+.4),q.y-8*Math.sin(ang+.4));ctx.closePath();ctx.fill();}
